.TH WINE-LAUNCHER 1 "2025-11-13" "Wine Launcher 0.1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
wine-launcher \- Run Windows applications on Linux using Wine/Proton

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wine-launcher
[\fIoptions\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wine-launcher
is a graphical application for managing Wine prefixes (called "bottles") and running Windows executables (.exe) on Linux. It provides a modern Qt6 interface for:

.IP •  4
Creating and managing isolated Wine prefixes (bottles)
.IP •  4
Detecting and selecting Wine/Proton runners (System Wine, Steam Proton, Proton-GE, Wine-GE, Custom)
.IP •  4
Installing Windows dependencies via Winetricks (libraries, runtime, settings)
.IP •  4
Enabling graphics translation layers (DXVK, VKD3D, dgVoodoo2)
.IP •  4
Backing up and restoring bottles
.IP •  4
Managing per-bottle environment variables and launch options

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--version\fR
Display version information and exit.

.TP
\fB--help\fR
Display help message and exit.

.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
\fBCtrl+N\fR
Create new bottle

.TP
\fBCtrl+R\fR
Run installed application in selected bottle

.TP
\fBCtrl+E\fR
Run custom executable in selected bottle

.TP
\fBCtrl+W\fR
Open Winetricks dialog for selected bottle

.TP
\fBCtrl+B\fR
Backup selected bottle

.TP
\fBCtrl+,\fR
Open settings dialog

.TP
\fBDelete\fR
Delete selected bottle

.TP
\fBF5\fR
Refresh bottle list

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/wine-launcher/config.json\fR
Global configuration (paths, defaults, UI preferences)

.TP
\fI~/.local/share/wine-launcher/bottles/\fR
Wine prefixes (one directory per bottle)

.TP
\fI~/.local/share/wine-launcher/backups/\fR
Compressed bottle backups (.tar.gz)

.TP
\fI~/.local/share/wine-launcher/runners/\fR
Custom runner installations

.TP
\fI~/.local/share/applications/wine-launcher.desktop\fR
Desktop entry for application menu

.TP
\fI~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/wine-launcher.png\fR
Application icon

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
\fBWINEDEBUG\fR
Wine debug channels (e.g., \fBWINEDEBUG=+all\fR, \fBWINEDEBUG=err+all\fR)

.TP
\fBWINEPREFIX\fR
Override Wine prefix path (set automatically per bottle)

.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Must include \fI~/.local/bin\fR for command-line access

.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP •  4
Linux kernel 5.10+
.IP •  4
Wine 8.0+ or Proton (install via system package manager)
.IP •  4
winetricks (optional, for dependency management)
.IP •  4
Vulkan-capable GPU + drivers (for DXVK/VKD3D)
.IP •  4
32-bit libraries (for 32-bit Windows apps)

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the GUI:
.B wine-launcher

.TP
Run with Wine debug output:
.B WINEDEBUG=+all wine-launcher 2>&1 | tee wine.log

.TP
Show version:
.B wine-launcher --version

